---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CategoryHub from '../../components/CategoryHub.astro';
import AffiliateDisclosure from '../../components/AffiliateDisclosure.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Forms & operations software for nonprofits"
  description="monday.com and Jotform for nonprofit operations: program tracking, intake forms, registrations, and the work that holds a shop together."
  section="forms-ops">
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Forms & operations' }]} />
    <section class="prose" style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">
      <p class="kicker">Category guide</p>
      <h1>Forms &amp; other operations</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The operational layer: program applications, volunteer intake, event
        registrations, and the lists and projects that hold a shop together.
        It's the cheapest category in the stack, and often the first one a
        grassroots shop actually pays for.
      </p>

      <AffiliateDisclosure />


      <h2>How to choose</h2>
      <p>
        Start with where the mess is. If it is <em>work</em> (grant deadlines,
        program tracking, who owes what by when), that is
        <a href="/go/monday" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">monday.com</a>:
        a free two-seat plan, paid plans from about $9 per seat, and a nonprofit
        program with discounted pricing. If it is <em>intake</em> (program
        applications, volunteer sign-ups, scholarship forms), that is
        <a href="/go/jotform" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">Jotform</a>:
        a capable free tier and a permanent 50% nonprofit discount that brings
        paid plans to roughly $17 a month.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most shops end up with both, and they cost less together than one seat
        of almost anything else in the stack. One discipline keeps this category
        from becoming a liability: anything you learn about a donor belongs in
        the <a href="/donor-crm/">donor CRM</a>, and donations belong on a
        <a href="/donation-processing/">giving platform</a>. Boards and forms are
        for operations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <CategoryHub category="forms-ops" />

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Ops tooling appears in every tier, starting free in
        <a href="/stacks/under-250k/">the grassroots stack</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
